{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310644,"nonce":"uwNJ+Ad88U6z09ORgW4uk8vEICg=","title":"OPEN, ONE defect behind ALL EIGHT gate known-fails: `new` in a loop body is freed at body scope exit while it escapes; the accumulator ...","message":"```haxe\nvar head:Node = null;\nfor (i in 0...3) { var n = new Node(i); n.next = head; head = n; }\n// rayzor: head.next == head  TRUE   (haxe 4.3.6: false)\n```\n`var n = new Node(i)` makes the loop body's drop scope the OWNER of `n`. MIR shows\n`free $13` at the end of the body, so malloc hands the identical 24-byte block back\nnext iteration. Any `while (p != null)` walk over the result never terminates —\na 300k-node build HANGS FOREVER (haxe does it in 0.24s).\n\nNOT an optimizer pass: reproduces with all ten disabled\n(`RAYZOR_DISABLE_PASSES=constant-folding,control-flow-simplification,copy-propagation,cse,dead-code-elimination,gvn,licm,strip-stack-trace-updates,tail-call-optimization,unreachable-block-elimination`).\n`RAYZOR_DISABLE_PASSES=all` matches NO pass name and disables NOTHING.\n\n`exit_drop_scope` (mir/helpers/drops.rs) already defers loop-carried symbols, but that\nprotects `head`; the free comes from `n`'s scope entry naming the SAME IrId. The tempting\nfix — in the `HirStatement::Assign` arm, when lhs is in `loop_carried_symbols.last()` and\nrhs is an owned Variable, move ownership rhs→lhs — was COMMITTED AND REVERTED. Measured\nfailures (all reproduced, `scratchpad/reverted/*.patch` has the diff):\n\n1. **DOUBLE FREE.** `@:derive(Drop)` + `var alias = head;` + `head = new Node(99)` prints\n   `drop 99` TWICE. The move's `already_owned` guard does not coordinate with\n   `register_owned_value` (mir/decl/init.rs:407-426); once anything untracks the symbol\n   between them, both take their \"first owner\" branch and the symbol gets TWO entries in\n   ONE scope. `exit_drop_scope` is immune (it removes from owned_heap_values) but\n   `cleanup_all_scopes_except_symbol` / `cleanup_drop_classes_only` are NOT — no dedup.\n2. **CATASTROPHIC LEAK.** The move untracks rhs at LOWERING time, unconditionally, but the\n   assignment can be CONDITIONAL at runtime (`if (cand.v \u003e best.v) best = cand;`).\n   `lower_if_statement` never saves/restores the tracker, so the not-taken path loses its\n   free too. Measured peak: HEAD 11.7 MB flat vs 3,272 MB at n=2M (and 66 GB at n=200k).\n3. **Incomplete.** Still broken, verified against the oracle: a `static var` accumulator\n   (the whole block is gated `if !lhs_is_global`) and a non-Variable RHS\n   (`head = (i\u003e=0) ? n : head` — it pattern-matches `HirExprKind::Variable` only).\n\nAny real fix must be CONDITIONAL-SAFE (runtime, not lowering-time), dedup scope entries,\nand cover global LHS + wrapped RHS. See [[reference_ownership_escape_routes_audited]].\n\n\n`scripts/check_ownership_gate.sh` KNOWN_FAIL is now local_accumulator,\nparam_accumulator, static_accumulator, ternary_rhs, array_push, capture_cell,\nshapes_guarded_while_nested, mem_accumulator_dies. Every one prints the collapsed\nanswer (`2 2 true` / `20 5 false` / `3 100 100`), and mem_accumulator_dies is the\nsame thing from the other side — the walk over the cyclic list never terminates,\nso it yields NO footprint. The list shrinks together or not at all.\n\nparam_accumulator USED to fail differently (trap stub, W0020) — that was a separate\nSSA bug, FIXED ffda0925 (see [[bugs_loop_assigned_parameter_no_phi]]). It now fails\nlike its siblings.\n\n`capped_run` backgrounded a SUBSHELL, so `kill` orphaned rayzor, the orphan held the\ncommand substitution's pipe open, and the caller blocked forever on a process the\nwatchdog had already killed. Cost ~2h across two runs. Now `exec`s rayzor so the pid\nIS rayzor, plus a `RUN_LIMIT_S` wall-clock ceiling (default 120s) on both capped_run\nand peak_mb. **A memory cap cannot catch a loop that allocates nothing.**\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): OPEN: `new` in a loop body returns the SAME address every iteration (linked list collapses, 300k-node build HANGS). The obvious ownership-move fix was COMMITTED AND REVERTED: double-free + 3.2GB leak. Design constraints inside.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_loop_body_alloc_aliases_every_iteration` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}